IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Paid Parental Leave Act 2010 (Commonwealth), compilation C2026C00425: the periods, dates, counts and amounts of
-- Chapter 2 Parts 2-1 to 2-3 Division 4 (sections 7 to 44), computed in one self-contained module.
-- It imports only prelude and daydate. Dates are written `Date day month year`.
-- The text does not say how a "second birthday" is reached for a child born on 29 February; the answer there is NOTHING.
-- A "week" is taken as seven days (the text does not define it).
-- Where a case is outside what the text states, a function answers NOTHING (a MAYBE result) and a test asserts it.

§ `Part 2-1 -- Key provisions`

-- src:381 | (b) ends on the day before the child’s second birthday.
@ref s 11D(b), the child's second birthday (src:381-381)
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the second birthday of a child born on` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH born EQUALS 2 AND DATE_DAY born EQUALS 29 AND (NOT `is leap year` (DATE_YEAR born PLUS 2))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (Date (DATE_DAY born) (DATE_MONTH born) (DATE_YEAR born PLUS 2))

-- src:381 | (b) ends on the day before the child’s second birthday.
@ref s 11D(b), the last flexible PPL day: the day before the child's second birthday (src:381-381)
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last flexible PPL day for a child born on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the second birthday of a child born on` born
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST birthday THEN JUST (birthday MINUS 1)

-- src:381 | (b) ends on the day before the child’s second birthday.
@ref s 11D(b), the period ends on the day before the child's second birthday (src:381-381)
GIVEN day IS A DATE, `the last day` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a day is no later than the last flexible PPL day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the last day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN JUST (day AT MOST lastDay)

-- src:379 | A day is a flexible PPL day for a child if the day occurs in the period that:
-- src:380 | (a) starts on the day the child is born; and
-- src:381 | (b) ends on the day before the child’s second birthday.
@ref s 11D, a day is a flexible PPL day for a child if it occurs in the period that starts on the birth and ends the day before the second birthday (src:379-381)
GIVEN day IS A DATE, born IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a day is a flexible PPL day for a child born on` MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN born
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `a day is no later than the last flexible PPL day` day (`the last flexible PPL day for a child born on` born)

§ `Part 2-2 -- Determinations`

-- src:518 | If a person is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to a claim for parental leave pay for a child of the person, the Secretary must not make a payability determination that parental leave pay is payable to the person for the child if the child is born after 31 March 2021.
@ref s 19B, the child is born after 31 March 2021 (src:518-518)
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a child is born after 31 March 2021` MEANS
    born GREATER THAN (Date 31 3 2021)

-- src:525 | (a) the effect of one or more payability determinations made by the Secretary under section 13 or 14 is that parental leave pay is payable to more than one person for the same flexible PPL day for the child on a total of:
-- src:526 | (i) if the child is born before 1 July 2025—10 flexible PPL days; or
-- src:527 | (ii) if the child is born on or after 1 July 2025—20 flexible PPL days; and
@ref s 21(1)(a)(i)-(ii), the total of flexible PPL days that stops a further determination, by the child's birth (src:525-527)
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total of flexible PPL days for more than one person, for a child born on` MEANS
    IF born LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2025)
    THEN 10
    ELSE 20

-- src:487 | (d) the variation of the permission does not affect the operation of the payability determination in relation to the days specified in the payability determination that, at the time the permission is varied, have already occurred; and
-- src:488 | (e) the Secretary must vary the payability determination to remove the days specified in the payability determination that, at the time the permission is varied:
-- src:489 | (i) have not yet occurred; and
-- src:498 | (d) the revocation of the permission does not affect the operation of the payability determination in relation to the days specified in the payability determination that, at the time the permission is revoked, have already occurred; and
-- src:499 | (e) the Secretary must vary the payability determination to remove the days specified in the payability determination that, at the time the permission is revoked, have not yet occurred; and
@ref s 15(6)(d)-(e) and (7)(d)-(e), a day that has already occurred or has not yet occurred when the permission is varied or revoked (src:487-499)
GIVEN day IS A DATE, `the day of the variation or revocation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a day has already occurred when the permission is varied or revoked` MEANS
    BRANCH IF day LESS THAN `the day of the variation or revocation` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF day GREATER THAN `the day of the variation or revocation` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:488 | (e) the Secretary must vary the payability determination to remove the days specified in the payability determination that, at the time the permission is varied:
-- src:489 | (i) have not yet occurred; and
-- src:490 | (ii) exceed the number of days specified in the permission, as varied; and
@ref s 15(6)(e), days of the determination to be removed: those not yet occurred that exceed the number specified in the varied permission (src:488-490)
GIVEN `days payable under the determination` IS A NUMBER, `days that have not yet occurred` IS A NUMBER, `the number specified in the permission as varied` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days removed from the determination on a variation` MEANS
    min `days that have not yet occurred` (max 0 (`days payable under the determination` MINUS `the number specified in the permission as varied`))

-- src:534 | A payability determination about parental leave pay comes into force on the day it is made and continues in force unless it is:
@ref s 23, a determination comes into force on the day it is made (src:534-534)
GIVEN `the day the determination is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a payability determination comes into force` MEANS `the day the determination is made`

-- src:547 | (c) the request is made before the last day of the instalment period for the instalment that relates to the flexible PPL day for the child; and
@ref s 25(1)(c), the request is made before the last day of the instalment period (src:547-547)
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE, `the last day of the instalment period` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a request to revoke is made before the last day of the instalment period` MEANS
    `the day of the request` LESS THAN `the last day of the instalment period`

-- src:550 | (2) The revocation is taken to have come into force on the day the person requested the Secretary to revoke the determination.
@ref s 25(2), the revocation is taken to come into force on the day the person requested it (src:550-550)
GIVEN `the day of the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a revocation is taken to come into force` MEANS `the day of the request`

-- src:560 | An initial eligibility determination about parental leave pay comes into force on the day it is made.
@ref s 28, an initial eligibility determination comes into force on the day it is made (src:560-560)
GIVEN `the day the determination is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day an initial eligibility determination comes into force` MEANS `the day the determination is made`

§ `Part 2-3 Division 2 -- When a person is eligible`

-- src:643 | (1) For the purposes of subsections 31AB(2), (4) and (5), the number of flexible PPL days for a child is:
-- src:644 | (a) for a child born before 1 July 2024—100 flexible PPL days for the child; or
-- src:645 | (b) for a child born between 1 July 2024 and 30 June 2025—110 flexible PPL days for the child; or
-- src:646 | (c) for a child born between 1 July 2025 and 30 June 2026—120 flexible PPL days for the child; or
-- src:647 | (d) for a child born on or after 1 July 2026—130 flexible PPL days for the child.
@ref s 31ABA(1)(a)-(d), the total limit of flexible PPL days for a child (src:643-647)
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total limit of flexible PPL days for a child born on` MEANS
    BRANCH IF born LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2024) THEN 100
           IF born AT MOST (Date 30 6 2025) THEN 110
           IF born AT MOST (Date 30 6 2026) THEN 120
           OTHERWISE 130

-- src:651 | (2) For the purposes of subsections 31AB(3) and (6), the number of flexible PPL days for a child is:
-- src:652 | (a) for a child born before 1 July 2024—90 flexible PPL days for the child; or
-- src:653 | (b) for a child born between 1 July 2024 and 30 June 2025—100 flexible PPL days for the child; or
-- src:654 | (c) for a child born between 1 July 2025 and 30 June 2026—105 flexible PPL days for the child; or
-- src:655 | (d) for a child born on or after 1 July 2026—110 flexible PPL days for the child.
@ref s 31ABA(2)(a)-(d), the claimant limit when partnered (reserved period) (src:651-655)
GIVEN born IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the claimant limit of flexible PPL days when partnered, for a child born on` MEANS
    BRANCH IF born LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2024) THEN 90
           IF born AT MOST (Date 30 6 2025) THEN 100
           IF born AT MOST (Date 30 6 2026) THEN 105
           OTHERWISE 110

-- src:673 | (e) ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
-- src:679 | (d) ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
-- src:686 | whichever occurs last, and ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
@ref s 31A(2)(e), (3)(d) and (4), the waiting period ends when the person has been in Australia for 104 weeks after the start day (src:673-686)
GIVEN `days in Australia after the start day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a newly arrived resident's waiting period has ended` MEANS
    `days in Australia after the start day` AT LEAST 104 TIMES 7

-- src:683 | the waiting period starts on the day on which the person:
-- src:684 | (c) first entered Australia; or
-- src:685 | (d) becomes the holder of a permanent visa;
-- src:686 | whichever occurs last, and ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
@ref s 31A(4)(c)-(d), the waiting period starts on whichever of first entering Australia and becoming the holder of a permanent visa occurs last (src:683-686)
GIVEN `the day the person first entered Australia` IS A DATE, `the day the person became the holder of a permanent visa` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day a newly arrived resident's waiting period starts under subsection (4)` MEANS
    IF `the day the person first entered Australia` AT LEAST `the day the person became the holder of a permanent visa`
    THEN `the day the person first entered Australia`
    ELSE `the day the person became the holder of a permanent visa`

-- src:667 | (2) If:
-- src:668 | (a) a person is subject to a newly arrived resident’s waiting period; and
-- src:669 | (b) the visa covered by paragraph (1)(a) or (b) is in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of paragraph 739A(3)(b) of the Social Security Act; and
-- src:670 | (c) subsection (3) does not apply;
-- src:671 | the waiting period:
-- src:672 | (d) starts on the day on which the person applied for that visa; and
-- src:673 | (e) ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
-- src:674 | (3) If:
-- src:675 | (a) a person is subject to a newly arrived resident’s waiting period; and
-- src:676 | (b) the person has previously held one or more visas in a class of visas determined by the Minister for the purposes of paragraph 739A(4)(b) of the Social Security Act;
-- src:677 | the waiting period:
-- src:678 | (c) starts on the day on which the person applied for the last of those visas; and
-- src:679 | (d) ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
-- src:680 | (4) If:
-- src:681 | (a) a person is subject to a newly arrived resident’s waiting period; and
-- src:682 | (b) neither subsection (2) nor (3) applies to the person;
-- src:683 | the waiting period starts on the day on which the person:
-- src:684 | (c) first entered Australia; or
-- src:685 | (d) becomes the holder of a permanent visa;
-- src:686 | whichever occurs last, and ends when the person has been in Australia for a period of, or periods totalling, 104 weeks after that day.
@ref s 31A(2)-(4), a day is in the waiting period from the start day until the person has been in Australia for 104 weeks after it (src:667-686)
GIVEN day IS A DATE, `the start day` IS A DATE, `days in Australia after the start day and before the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a day is in a newly arrived resident's waiting period` MEANS
        day AT LEAST `the start day`
    AND NOT `a newly arrived resident's waiting period has ended` `days in Australia after the start day and before the day`

-- src:698 | (b) a person has made an effective claim for parental leave pay for a period of at least 10 flexible PPL days for a child; and
@ref s 31A(6B)(b), a period of at least 10 flexible PPL days (src:698-698)
GIVEN `flexible PPL days in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the claim is for a period of at least 10 flexible PPL days` MEANS
    `flexible PPL days in the period` AT LEAST 10

-- src:581 | (c) on that day the person is performing no more than one hour of paid work; and
@ref s 31AA(2)(c), no more than one hour of paid work on the day (src:581-581)
GIVEN `hours of paid work on the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the hours of paid work on the day are no more than one` MEANS
    `hours of paid work on the day` AT MOST 1

-- src:613 | (a) one or more determinations under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to a person are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(1); and
-- src:618 | (b) one or more determinations under section 13 that parental leave pay is payable to the relevant claimant are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(2); and
-- src:623 | (a) one or more determinations under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to the relevant claimant or the relevant claimant’s partner (if any) are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(1); and
-- src:628 | (a) one or more determinations under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to the relevant claimant or the relevant claimant’s partner (if any) are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(1); and
-- src:634 | (b) one or more determinations under section 13 or 14 that parental leave pay is payable to the relevant claimant are in force in relation to the number of flexible PPL days for the child specified in subsection 31ABA(2); and
@ref s 31AB(2)(a), (3)(b), (4)(a), (5)(a) and (6)(b), determinations are in force for the number of flexible PPL days that the limit specifies (src:613-634)
GIVEN `flexible PPL days covered by determinations in force` IS A NUMBER, limit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`determinations in force cover the number of flexible PPL days that the limit specifies` MEANS
    `flexible PPL days covered by determinations in force` AT LEAST limit

§ `Part 1-2 -- Definitions in numbers`

-- src:142 | born prematurely: a child is born prematurely if, at the time of the child’s delivery, the child’s period of gestation is less than 37 weeks.
@ref s 6, born prematurely: the child's period of gestation is less than 37 weeks (src:142-142)
GIVEN `weeks of gestation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the period of gestation is less than 37 weeks` MEANS
    `weeks of gestation` LESS THAN 37

-- src:326 | (a) who weighs at least 400 grams at delivery or whose period of gestation was at least 20 weeks; and
@ref s 6, stillborn (a): weighs at least 400 grams at delivery or the period of gestation was at least 20 weeks (src:326-326)
GIVEN `weight at delivery in grams` IS A NUMBER, `weeks of gestation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the child weighed at least 400 grams or the gestation was at least 20 weeks` MEANS
    `weight at delivery in grams` AT LEAST 400 OR `weeks of gestation` AT LEAST 20

-- src:165 | (a) either:
-- src:166 | (i) the child is or was born between 22 March 2020 and 31 March 2021; or
-- src:167 | (ii) if the claim is made before the child’s birth—the child’s expected date of birth is during that period; and
@ref s 6, COVID-19 affected claimant (a)(i)-(ii): the child is born, or is expected to be born, between 22 March 2020 and 31 March 2021 (src:165-167)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a day is between 22 March 2020 and 31 March 2021` MEANS
    day AT LEAST (Date 22 3 2020) AND day AT MOST (Date 31 3 2021)

-- src:352 | week day means a day that is not a Saturday or a Sunday.
@ref s 6, week day: a day that is not a Saturday or a Sunday (src:352-352)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a day is a week day` MEANS
    `is weekday` day

§ `Part 2-3 Division 3 -- The work test`

-- src:728 | Step 4. Work out whether there is a period (a qualifying period) of 295 consecutive days in the work test period that are days:
@ref s 32 Step 4, a qualifying period is 295 consecutive days (src:728-728)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of consecutive days in a qualifying period` MEANS 295

-- src:731 | Step 5. If the person has performed at least 330 hours of qualifying work in a qualifying period, the person satisfies the work test.
@ref s 32 Step 5, at least 330 hours of qualifying work in a qualifying period (src:731-731)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours of qualifying work needed in a qualifying period` MEANS 330

-- src:746 | (1) The work test period for the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the 392 days immediately before:
-- src:756 | (2) However, for the purposes of making an initial eligibility determination on a PPL claim or special PPL claim, the work test period for the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the 392 days immediately before:
-- src:768 | The work test period for a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant who is a COVID-19 affected claimant in relation to a claim for parental leave pay for a child is the work test period that would apply to the claimant under section 33 if:
-- src:769 | (a) subsection 33(1A) were disregarded; and
-- src:770 | (b) the reference in subsections 33(1) and (2) to 392 days were a reference to 600 days.
@ref s 33(1) and (2), the work test period is 392 days; s 33A, it is 600 days for a COVID-19 affected claimant (src:746-770)
GIVEN `the claimant is a COVID-19 affected claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days in the work test period` MEANS
    IF `the claimant is a COVID-19 affected claimant` THEN 600 ELSE 392

-- src:746 | (1) The work test period for the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the 392 days immediately before:
-- src:747 | (a) if:
-- src:748 | (i) subsection (2A) applies in relation to the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant; and
-- src:749 | (ii) the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant would not satisfy the work test if the claimant’s work test period were the work test period under paragraph (b) or (c) of this subsection;
-- src:750 | the claimant’s work cessation day; or
-- src:751 | (b) if:
-- src:752 | (i) the child of the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is born after the expected date of birth of the child; and
-- src:753 | (ii) the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant would not satisfy the work test if the claimant’s work test period were the work test period under paragraph (c) of this subsection;
-- src:754 | the expected date of birth of the child; or
-- src:755 | (c) otherwise—the day the child is born.
-- src:756 | (2) However, for the purposes of making an initial eligibility determination on a PPL claim or special PPL claim, the work test period for the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the 392 days immediately before:
-- src:757 | (a) if:
-- src:758 | (i) subsection (2A) applies in relation to the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant; and
-- src:759 | (ii) the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant would not satisfy the work test if the claimant’s work test period were the work test period under paragraph (b) of this subsection;
-- src:760 | the claimant’s work cessation day; or
-- src:761 | (b) otherwise—the expected date of birth of the child.
@ref s 33(1)(a)-(c) and (2)(a)-(b), the day from which the work test period is counted back (src:746-761)
GIVEN `for an initial eligibility determination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2A) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant's work cessation day` IS A DATE
      `the claimant would not satisfy the work test with the period that would otherwise apply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child is born after the expected date of birth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant would not satisfy the work test with the period counted back from the day the child is born` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expected date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day the child is born` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the work test period is counted back from` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `for an initial eligibility determination` AND `subsection (2A) applies` AND `the claimant would not satisfy the work test with the period that would otherwise apply`
           THEN `the claimant's work cessation day`
           IF `for an initial eligibility determination`
           THEN `the expected date of birth`
           IF `subsection (2A) applies` AND `the claimant would not satisfy the work test with the period that would otherwise apply`
           THEN `the claimant's work cessation day`
           IF `the child is born after the expected date of birth` AND `the claimant would not satisfy the work test with the period counted back from the day the child is born`
           THEN `the expected date of birth`
           OTHERWISE `the day the child is born`

-- src:746 | (1) The work test period for the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the 392 days immediately before:
-- src:756 | (2) However, for the purposes of making an initial eligibility determination on a PPL claim or special PPL claim, the work test period for the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the 392 days immediately before:
@ref s 33(1) and (2), the work test period is the days immediately before the day: its first day (src:746-756)
GIVEN `the day counted back from` IS A DATE, `the number of days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day of the work test period` MEANS
    `the day counted back from` MINUS `the number of days`

-- src:746 | (1) The work test period for the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the 392 days immediately before:
-- src:756 | (2) However, for the purposes of making an initial eligibility determination on a PPL claim or special PPL claim, the work test period for the PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the 392 days immediately before:
@ref s 33(1) and (2), the work test period is the days immediately before the day: its last day (src:746-756)
GIVEN `the day counted back from` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the work test period` MEANS
    `the day counted back from` MINUS 1

-- src:831 | (2) If, between a day on which the person performed qualifying work (a qualifying work day) in the work test period and the next qualifying work day, there was at least 1 day but not more than 84 consecutive days on which the person did not perform qualifying work—the day or period of consecutive days between those 2 qualifying work days is a permissible break.
@ref s 36(2), a permissible break between two qualifying work days is at least 1 day but not more than 84 consecutive days (src:831-831)
GIVEN `consecutive days with no qualifying work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the days between two qualifying work days are a permissible break` MEANS
    `consecutive days with no qualifying work` AT LEAST 1 AND `consecutive days with no qualifying work` AT MOST 84

-- src:836 | (c) the later qualifying work day was no more than 84 consecutive days after the earlier qualifying work day;
@ref s 36(3)(c), the later qualifying work day was no more than 84 consecutive days after the earlier (src:836-836)
GIVEN `the earlier qualifying work day` IS A DATE, `the later qualifying work day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the later qualifying work day is no more than 84 days after the earlier` MEANS
    (`the later qualifying work day` MINUS `the earlier qualifying work day`) AT MOST 84

-- src:803 | (1) For the purposes of step 5 of the method statement in section 32, if a person performs qualifying work on a day only because the day is a flexible PPL day for a previous child, the person is taken to have performed 7.6 hours of work on that day.
@ref s 35A(1), a day that is qualifying work only because it is a flexible PPL day for a previous child counts as 7.6 hours (src:803-803)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours taken for a flexible PPL day for a previous child` MEANS 7.6

-- src:773 | (a) the person performs at least one hour of paid work;
-- src:774 | (b) the person takes a period of paid leave of at least one hour;
@ref s 34(1)(a)-(b), at least one hour of paid work or paid leave (src:773-774)
GIVEN hours IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`at least one hour` MEANS
    hours AT LEAST 1

§ `Part 2-3 Division 4 -- The income test`

-- src:892 | (a) if the day is on or after 1 October 2010 but before 1 July 2021—$150,000; and
@ref s 41(1)(a), the individual PPL income limit is $150,000 from 1 October 2010 to before 1 July 2021 (src:892-892)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the individual limit stated for a day` MEANS
    IF day AT LEAST (Date 1 10 2010) AND day LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2021)
    THEN JUST 150000
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:895 | (a) if the day is on or after 1 July 2023 but before 1 July 2024—$350,000; and
@ref s 41(2)(a), the family PPL income limit is $350,000 from 1 July 2023 to before 1 July 2024 (src:895-895)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the family limit stated for a day` MEANS
    IF day AT LEAST (Date 1 7 2023) AND day LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2024)
    THEN JUST 350000
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `December quarter index` HAS
    `the year of the December quarter` IS A NUMBER
    `the index number` IS A NUMBER

-- src:900 | (1) Subject to subsection (2), the amount of the individual PPL income limit and the amount of the family PPL income limit are to be indexed under this Subdivision on 1 July each year (the indexation day).
-- src:901 | (2) The first indexation day for an amount of the individual PPL income limit is 1 July 2021 and the first indexation day for an amount of the family PPL income limit is 1 July 2024.
@ref s 42(1), the indexation day is 1 July each year; s 42(2), the first for the individual limit is 1 July 2021 and for the family limit 1 July 2024 (src:900-901)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of the 1 July on or before a day` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH day AT LEAST 7 THEN DATE_YEAR day ELSE DATE_YEAR day MINUS 1

-- src:914 | reference December quarter means the last December quarter before the indexation day.
@ref s 43(1), the reference December quarter is the last December quarter before the indexation day (src:914-914)
GIVEN `the year of the indexation day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the year of the reference December quarter` MEANS
    `the year of the indexation day` MINUS 1

-- src:912 | base December quarter means the December quarter that has the highest index number of the December quarters before the reference December quarter (but not earlier than the December quarter 2007).
@ref s 43(1), the base December quarter is the one with the highest index number of those before the reference quarter, not earlier than the December quarter 2007 (src:912-912)
GIVEN `the year of the reference December quarter` IS A NUMBER, quarters IS A LIST OF `December quarter index`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the index number of the base December quarter` MEANS
    maximum (map (GIVEN q YIELD q's `the index number`) (filter `is a candidate base quarter` quarters))
    WHERE
        `is a candidate base quarter` q MEANS
                q's `the year of the December quarter` LESS THAN `the year of the reference December quarter`
            AND q's `the year of the December quarter` AT LEAST 2007

-- src:910 | (1) The indexation factor is worked out using the following formula and applying subsections (2) and (3):
-- src:911 | where:
-- src:912 | base December quarter means the December quarter that has the highest index number of the December quarters before the reference December quarter (but not earlier than the December quarter 2007).
-- src:913 | index number, for a quarter, means the All Groups Consumer Price Index number that is the weighted average of the 8 capital cities and is published by the Australian Statistician in relation to that quarter.
-- src:914 | reference December quarter means the last December quarter before the indexation day.
@ref s 43(1), the indexation factor is the index number for the reference December quarter over the index number for the base December quarter (src:910-914)
GIVEN `the year of the reference December quarter` IS A NUMBER, quarters IS A LIST OF `December quarter index`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the index number of the reference December quarter` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN q YIELD q's `the index number`) (filter (GIVEN q YIELD q's `the year of the December quarter` EQUALS `the year of the reference December quarter`) quarters))

-- src:915 | (2) The indexation factor is to be worked out to 3 decimal places, but increased by 0.001 if the fourth decimal place is more than 4.
-- src:916 | (3) If an indexation factor worked out under subsections (1) and (2) would be less than 1, that indexation factor is to be increased to 1.
@ref s 43(2)-(3), the factor is worked out to 3 decimal places, increased by 0.001 if the fourth decimal place is more than 4, and increased to 1 if it would be less than 1 (src:915-916)
GIVEN ratio IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the indexation factor rounded` MEANS
    max 1 (`the factor to 3 decimal places` PLUS (IF `the fourth decimal place` GREATER THAN 4 THEN 0.001 ELSE 0))
    WHERE
        `the factor to 3 decimal places` MEANS TRUNC ratio 3
        `the fourth decimal place` MEANS (FLOOR (ratio TIMES 10000)) MODULO 10

-- src:922 | (1) If a provisional indexed amount is a multiple of $1.00, the provisional indexed amount becomes the indexed amount.
-- src:923 | (2) If a provisional indexed amount is not a multiple of $1.00, the indexed amount is the provisional indexed amount rounded up or down to the nearest multiple of $1.00.
-- src:924 | (3) If a provisional indexed amount is not a multiple of $1.00 but is a multiple of $0.50, the indexed amount is the provisional indexed amount rounded up to the nearest multiple of $1.00.
@ref s 44(1)-(3), rounding off an indexed amount (src:922-924)
GIVEN `the provisional indexed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the indexed amount` MEANS
    BRANCH IF FLOOR `the provisional indexed amount` EQUALS `the provisional indexed amount` THEN `the provisional indexed amount`
           IF FLOOR (`the provisional indexed amount` TIMES 2) EQUALS (`the provisional indexed amount` TIMES 2) THEN CEILING `the provisional indexed amount`
           OTHERWISE ROUND `the provisional indexed amount`

-- src:904 | Method statement
-- src:905 | Step 1. Work out the amount (the previous amount) for the relevant income limit that applied on the day immediately before the indexation day.
-- src:906 | Step 2. Use section 43 to work out the indexation factor on the indexation day.
-- src:907 | Step 3. Multiply the previous amount by the indexation factor: the result is the provisional indexed amount.
-- src:908 | Step 4. Use section 44 to round off the provisional indexed amount: the result is the indexed amount.
@ref s 42(3) Steps 1-4, the indexed amount on an indexation day (src:904-908)
GIVEN `the previous amount` IS A NUMBER, `the year of the indexation day` IS A NUMBER, quarters IS A LIST OF `December quarter index`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the indexed amount on an indexation day` MEANS
    `the indexed amount` (`the previous amount` TIMES `the indexation factor`)
    WHERE
        `the reference quarter year` MEANS `the year of the reference December quarter` `the year of the indexation day`
        -- The formula in section 43(1) is a picture that the text file does not carry; the sidecar C2026C00425.formulas.md transcribes it as
        -- the index number for the reference December quarter divided by the index number for the base December quarter.
        `the indexation factor` MEANS
            `the indexation factor rounded`
                (`the index number of the reference December quarter` `the reference quarter year` quarters
                    DIVIDED BY `the index number of the base December quarter` `the reference quarter year` quarters)

-- src:893 | (b) if the day is on or after an indexation day (the relevant indexation day) but before the next indexation day—the indexed amount on the relevant indexation day worked out under Subdivision B.
-- src:901 | (2) The first indexation day for an amount of the individual PPL income limit is 1 July 2021 and the first indexation day for an amount of the family PPL income limit is 1 July 2024.
@ref s 41(1)(b) and s 42(2), the individual limit on a day on or after the first indexation day is the indexed amount on the relevant indexation day (src:893-901)
GIVEN `the year of the indexation day` IS A NUMBER, quarters IS A LIST OF `December quarter index`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the individual limit after indexation in the year` MEANS
    IF `the year of the indexation day` LESS THAN 2021
    THEN 150000
    ELSE `the indexed amount on an indexation day` (`the individual limit after indexation in the year` (`the year of the indexation day` MINUS 1) quarters) `the year of the indexation day` quarters

-- src:896 | (b) if the day is on or after an indexation day (the relevant indexation day) but before the next indexation day—the indexed amount on the relevant indexation day worked out under Subdivision B.
-- src:901 | (2) The first indexation day for an amount of the individual PPL income limit is 1 July 2021 and the first indexation day for an amount of the family PPL income limit is 1 July 2024.
@ref s 41(2)(b) and s 42(2), the family limit on a day on or after the first indexation day is the indexed amount on the relevant indexation day (src:896-901)
GIVEN `the year of the indexation day` IS A NUMBER, quarters IS A LIST OF `December quarter index`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the family limit after indexation in the year` MEANS
    IF `the year of the indexation day` LESS THAN 2024
    THEN 350000
    ELSE `the indexed amount on an indexation day` (`the family limit after indexation in the year` (`the year of the indexation day` MINUS 1) quarters) `the year of the indexation day` quarters

-- src:891 | (1) The individual PPL income limit that applies on a day is:
-- src:892 | (a) if the day is on or after 1 October 2010 but before 1 July 2021—$150,000; and
-- src:893 | (b) if the day is on or after an indexation day (the relevant indexation day) but before the next indexation day—the indexed amount on the relevant indexation day worked out under Subdivision B.
@ref s 41(1), the individual PPL income limit that applies on a day (src:891-893)
GIVEN day IS A DATE, quarters IS A LIST OF `December quarter index`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the individual PPL income limit that applies on a day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF day LESS THAN (Date 1 10 2010) THEN NOTHING
           IF day LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2021) THEN `the individual limit stated for a day` day
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the individual limit after indexation in the year` (`the year of the 1 July on or before a day` day) quarters)

-- src:894 | (2) The family PPL income limit that applies on a day is:
-- src:895 | (a) if the day is on or after 1 July 2023 but before 1 July 2024—$350,000; and
-- src:896 | (b) if the day is on or after an indexation day (the relevant indexation day) but before the next indexation day—the indexed amount on the relevant indexation day worked out under Subdivision B.
@ref s 41(2), the family PPL income limit that applies on a day (src:894-896)
GIVEN day IS A DATE, quarters IS A LIST OF `December quarter index`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the family PPL income limit that applies on a day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF day LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2023) THEN NOTHING
           IF day LESS THAN (Date 1 7 2024) THEN `the family limit stated for a day` day
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the family limit after indexation in the year` (`the year of the 1 July on or before a day` day) quarters)

-- src:884 | (1) The relevant individual PPL income limit for a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the individual PPL income limit that applies on the earlier of the following days:
-- src:885 | (a) the day the person made the claim;
-- src:886 | (b) the day the child was born.
-- src:887 | (2) The relevant family PPL income limit for a PPL claimant or special PPL claimant is the family PPL income limit that applies on the earlier of the following days:
-- src:888 | (a) the day the person made the claim;
-- src:889 | (b) the day the child was born.
@ref s 40(1)-(2), the limit that applies on the earlier of the day the person made the claim and the day the child was born (src:884-889)
GIVEN `the day the person made the claim` IS A DATE, `the day the child was born` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of the claim day and the birth day` MEANS
    IF `the day the person made the claim` AT MOST `the day the child was born`
    THEN `the day the person made the claim`
    ELSE `the day the child was born`

-- src:879 | The reference income year for a person is:
-- src:880 | (a) the income year that ended before the earlier of:
-- src:881 | (i) the day the person made the claim; and
-- src:882 | (ii) the day the child was born.
@ref s 39, the reference income year is the income year that ended before the earlier of the claim day and the birth day (src:879-882)
GIVEN `the earlier day` IS A DATE, `the end days of the income years` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the end day of the reference income year` MEANS
    IF null `the earlier end days`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (Date (maximum (map (GIVEN d YIELD Day d) `the earlier end days`)))
    WHERE
        `the earlier end days` MEANS filter (GIVEN d YIELD d LESS THAN `the earlier day`) `the end days of the income years`
